  "term": "rich medium",
  "definition": "In this packet, a rich medium means a growth medium that contains abundant nutrients, especially protein hydrolysates such as casein digest. Here it refers to media with high levels of amino acids like proline and glutamate that were associated with programmed cell death in the bacterial cells studied.",
